Christine's bodies were found the next day partially buried in the sand. Both had suffered from multiple violent stab wounds caused by a knife amongst other injuries. Their murders came to be known as the Wanda Beach murders and remain one of the most infamous unsolved Australian murder cases. We covered the case in detail in case file episode number one. Based on his history, Alan Bassett was considered by at least one detective to be a prime suspect in the Wanda Beach murders. Bassett strongly denied any involvement and he even offered to give a DNA sample to prove his innocence. It's unknown if he was ever taken up on his offer. A blonde-haired young man described as a surfer was seen around Wanda Beach at the time of the

